      "writtenOn": "2022-07-22T12:17:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In general I would not recommend passing the profile in the constructor.\nIf a service depends on profile, it basically depends on all of the code, as the profile is almost a singleton. As the result the code is not encapsulated at all.\n\nI don\u0027t know if we could change that example, e.g:\n\n```\nclass FooService : public KeyedService {\n public:\n  FooService(PrefService* profile_prefs, BarService* bar_service);\n  virtual ~FooService() \u003d default;\n\n  FooService(const FooService\u0026) \u003d delete;\n  FooService\u0026 operator\u003d(const FooService\u0026) \u003d delete;\n\n private:\n  PrefService* profile_prefs_;\n  BarService* bar_service_;\n};\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 73,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 73,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "0801c827c1c1e30dba93a131ee21cc96f75323be",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
